We also implemented a “Kafka adapter” for Mofka. That is, the Mofka API can be used to interact with232
a deployment of Kafka, Redpanda, or any similar system satisfying the Kafka protocol. It does so by233
using librdkafka,2 a widely used C implementation of the Kafka protocol, and by adding Argobots-based234
threading on top of it to provide some of the features from the Mofka client library that are missing235
from librdkafka. Hence, HPC applications that use the Mofka API can also be tested on top of Kafka or236
Redpanda. We use this feature in particular for benchmarking against these systems in Section 4.237
3.4 Implementation and modularity238
As stated earlier, Mofka is built using the Mochi suite of technologies, which advertises a composable239
approach to the design of HPC data services, with reusable components at the center of such design.240
Figure 1 shows that Mofka servers are made of multiple components, only one of which is in fact241
exclusive to Mofka: the partition manager. The event log consists of a Yokan component,3 which provides242
key/value and document collection storage. The storage provider is a Warabi component,4 which provides243
blob storage functionality. Group membership is managed by Flock, 5, the master database is another244
